  "story": {
    "day": 130,
    "title": "Kaya's Northern Volunteer Trip",
    "sentences": [
      "Kaya worked on her own report in her bedroom.",
      "Her plan was a volunteer journey to a wild country.",
      "She remembered her fourteenth birthday, not her twelfth.",
      "She wanted to travel far away to see the aurora and wolves.",
      "Kaya went to the department store for shorts on sale.",
      "She took medicine, coffee, and a snack for their camp.",
      "She would carry them safely, being careful not to drop her number.",
      "A big Brown Bear walked close; she held out a letter.",
      "An interviewer asked her to answer about forty wild bear.",
      "They roasted food and had a fun laugh, despite the weather.",
      "Kaya was sure the culture would make a big difference.",
      "Her only break was a skate near the corner, she would not lose."
    ]
  }
}